  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342101",
      "title": "TypeScript: What & Why?",
      "lectureOrder": 495,
      "videoOrder": 437,
      "sourceHash": "c65f590d4ff6872175ed8fbfca684d7c1d57d79412d8bc97f677928cff8123f9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.28,
          "end": 4.48,
          "en": "So, what is TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.48,
          "end": 7.26,
          "en": "and why would we use it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.26,
          "end": 10.81,
          "en": "TypeScript is a superset to JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.81,
          "end": 13.92,
          "en": "That simply means that it extends JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.92,
          "end": 16.4,
          "en": "It builds up on JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.4,
          "end": 21.11,
          "en": "And unlike JavaScript, TypeScript does not run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.11,
          "end": 22.22,
          "en": "in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.22,
          "end": 26.93,
          "en": "Instead, TypeScript has to be compiled to JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.93,
          "end": 28.76,
          "en": "so that it runs again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.76,
          "end": 31.35,
          "en": "Now, why would we then work with it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.35,
          "end": 34.51,
          "en": "Because TypeScript gives us, as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.51,
          "end": 36.49,
          "en": "a better development experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.49,
          "end": 40.16,
          "en": "because it adds certain feature to the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.16,
          "end": 42.41,
          "en": "which only exist during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.41,
          "end": 45.56,
          "en": "but which still help us write better code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.56,
          "end": 48.74,
          "en": "and avoid unwanted errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.74,
          "end": 50.58,
          "en": "And here's an example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.58,
          "end": 53.06,
          "en": "This is a function, this is some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.06,
          "end": 55.73,
          "en": "where TypeScript can help you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.73,
          "end": 58.04,
          "en": "Now, what could be wrong about this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.04,
          "end": 60.49,
          "en": "Let's simply try it on our own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.49,
          "end": 63.42,
          "en": "For this, you can simply open up your developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.42,
          "end": 64.84,
          "en": "in Chrome, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.84,
          "end": 67.4,
          "en": "and there go to the JavaScript console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.4,
          "end": 70.73,
          "en": "In there, you can also write some basic JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.73,
          "end": 73.07,
          "en": "which will then be executed here in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.07,
          "end": 75.85,
          "en": "And, for this simple example, that's all we need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.85,
          "end": 79.4,
          "en": "So, in there, let's define a function now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.4,
          "end": 81.56,
          "en": "A function which is named add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.56,
          "end": 86.41,
          "en": "and which takes two parameters, num1 and num2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.41,
          "end": 88.06,
          "en": "Then, let's add curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.06,
          "end": 91,
          "en": "and now place your cursor between these braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91,
          "end": 93.55,
          "en": "and hit Shift + Enter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 93.55,
          "end": 95.513,
          "en": "This will then simply add a new line.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 96.44,
          "end": 99.36,
          "en": "Now, inside of that function, we can return the result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.36,
          "end": 102.49000000000001,
          "en": "num1 plus num2, just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.49000000000001,
          "end": 106.4,
          "en": "So, that's a very trivial function for adding two numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.4,
          "end": 109.15,
          "en": "If you now hit Enter without Shift,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.15,
          "end": 111.93,
          "en": "this code will be committed, it will be saved,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.93,
          "end": 116.06,
          "en": "and now this add function exists here in the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 116.06,
          "end": 118.85,
          "en": "Hence, we can now call add with one and five",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.85,
          "end": 120.4,
          "en": "and get back six.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.4,
          "end": 122.07,
          "en": "Seems to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.07,
          "end": 126.9,
          "en": "What if you would pass in one and five as strings though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.9,
          "end": 130.01,
          "en": "Then, you get back the string 15.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 130.01,
          "end": 135.01,
          "en": "So, one and five are then concatenated to one longer string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.52,
          "end": 138.15,
          "en": "instead of being converted to numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.15,
          "end": 140.65,
          "en": "and then added as numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.65,
          "end": 143.44,
          "en": "Now, the reason for this is that this is simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.44,
          "end": 145.13,
          "en": "how JavaScript works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.13,
          "end": 149.03,
          "en": "If you have an operation with a plus and at least one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.03,
          "end": 151.13,
          "en": "of the two operands is a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.13,
          "end": 155.26,
          "en": "then both will be combined as strings, essentially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.26,
          "end": 156.71,
          "en": "That's how JavaScript works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 156.71,
          "end": 159.36,
          "en": "And this, of course, can be a problem here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 159.36,
          "end": 163.28,
          "en": "Now, you might think that this is a unrealistic scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.28,
          "end": 166.52,
          "en": "because why would you call the function with two strings?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.52,
          "end": 170.5,
          "en": "Well, imagine that you have two inputs in your page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.5,
          "end": 173.68,
          "en": "Two inputs where you fetch some user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.68,
          "end": 177.38,
          "en": "Now, you should know that whatever data you extract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 177.38,
          "end": 182.38,
          "en": "from such inputs is always extracted as text in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.81,
          "end": 186.25,
          "en": "So, even if the user entered a number in an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.25,
          "end": 190.2,
          "en": "on your page, if you extract that data with JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.2,
          "end": 192.42,
          "en": "it'll be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.42,
          "end": 194.52,
          "en": "Now, you can always convert this to a number, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 194.52,
          "end": 198.27,
          "en": "but if you forget this, and you pass the unconverted value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.27,
          "end": 202.28300000000002,
          "en": "to this function, you might get this unintended result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.3,
          "end": 205.55,
          "en": "Now, that's where TypeScript can help us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.55,
          "end": 210.2,
          "en": "To avoid such a unwanted behavior which occurs at runtime,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.2,
          "end": 214.67000000000002,
          "en": "so when our code executes, we can use TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.67000000000002,
          "end": 217.64,
          "en": "Now, of course, we could also avoid this behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.64,
          "end": 219.77,
          "en": "at runtime with JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.77,
          "end": 221.81,
          "en": "We could add an if check, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.81,
          "end": 224.95,
          "en": "to see whether the values we received are strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 224.95,
          "end": 225.85,
          "en": "or numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 225.85,
          "end": 228.57999999999998,
          "en": "That is something we can check with JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.57999999999998,
          "end": 231.453,
          "en": "and this would allow us to avoid such mistakes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 231.453,
          "end": 234.67000000000002,
          "en": "but, of course, that means you have to write extra code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234.67000000000002,
          "end": 238.1,
          "en": "at runtime to make sure that your code works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 238.1,
          "end": 241.21,
          "en": "when you actually could avoid this during development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 241.21,
          "end": 243.98,
          "en": "if you had strict type checks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 243.98,
          "end": 247.15,
          "en": "So, if you simply could tell JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 247.15,
          "end": 251.24,
          "en": "so to say in advance which types of data you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.24,
          "end": 255.08,
          "en": "and then JavaScript and your IDE could warn you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 255.08,
          "end": 257.41,
          "en": "when you have some code in your program",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 257.41,
          "end": 260.19,
          "en": "where wrong types are fed in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 260.19,
          "end": 262.46,
          "en": "And that's where TypeScript helps us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 262.46,
          "end": 265.06,
          "en": "It adds strict typing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 265.06,
          "end": 268.35,
          "en": "In general, TypeScript adds a bunch of features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 268.35,
          "end": 269.79,
          "en": "to JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 269.79,
          "end": 273.25,
          "en": "It adds the types, and that's the most important addition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 273.25,
          "end": 276.72,
          "en": "That's where TypeScript's name comes from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 276.72,
          "end": 278.55,
          "en": "But it also unlocks certain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 278.55,
          "end": 281.15,
          "en": "next-generation JavaScript features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 281.15,
          "end": 283.22,
          "en": "which we then can use in our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 283.22,
          "end": 286.63,
          "en": "without any extra tools like Babel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 286.63,
          "end": 290.28,
          "en": "It also adds some non next-gen features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 290.28,
          "end": 293.79,
          "en": "so some features which don't exist in JavaScript at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 293.79,
          "end": 296.3,
          "en": "which help us write cleaner code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 296.3,
          "end": 298.56,
          "en": "Now, all these features are stripped away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 298.56,
          "end": 300.67,
          "en": "once it's compiled, but during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 300.67,
          "end": 304.35,
          "en": "those features can help us write cleaner code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 304.35,
          "end": 307.72,
          "en": "It adds meta-programming features like Decorators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 307.72,
          "end": 310.43,
          "en": "It has rich configuration options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 310.43,
          "end": 313.23,
          "en": "that allow us as a developer to fine-tune",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 313.23,
          "end": 315.1,
          "en": "how code should be compiled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 315.1,
          "end": 318.93,
          "en": "And it, in general, simply gives us a lot of modern tooling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 318.93,
          "end": 322.3,
          "en": "and integrates greatly into modern tooling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 322.3,
          "end": 325.33,
          "en": "to give us a great development experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 325.33,
          "end": 328.75,
          "en": "Now, in this basics refresher here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 328.75,
          "end": 333.24,
          "en": "I'm not going to dive into all these areas in great detail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 333.24,
          "end": 334.40999999999997,
          "en": "For that, you can check out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 334.40999999999997,
          "end": 336.87,
          "en": "my Understanding TypeScript course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 336.87,
          "end": 340.13,
          "en": "This course dives into TypeScript in great detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 340.13,
          "end": 343.56,
          "en": "and walks you through all the core features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 343.56,
          "end": 344.77,
          "en": "So, that's my recommendation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 344.77,
          "end": 347.40999999999997,
          "en": "if you wanna learn all about TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 347.40999999999997,
          "end": 350.5,
          "en": "Here, we're going to dive into some core basics.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 350.5,
          "end": 352.81,
          "en": "And, for that, let's actually come back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 352.81,
          "end": 355.21,
          "en": "to this example I just showed you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 355.21,
